  "limitations": [
    "ablation_effect in head_ablation_results.parquet is all-NaN with ablation_scope='unset': Phases 4-5 have produced no SignificanceMatrix to attach.",
    "patch_effect is a LAYER quantity, not a head quantity: attn_out is captured after o_proj, where the heads have already been summed.",
    "span_aligned patches move the evidence's content and its RoPE phase together; a positive effect cannot be attributed to either alone. random_control bounds the amount-of-substitution part only.",
    "Probes are correlational. A high R^2 nominates a layer for patching; it is not evidence the forward pass uses that information.",
    "answer_identity_full is expected to report status='skipped' on this bank: answers are unique per scenario, so a by-scenario split leaves every test class unseen. answer_identity_first_token is near-degenerate for the same reason (measured on the calibration 4K bank: only two first-token classes appear in two or more scenarios, one of them covering ~70% of them), so read its accuracy against the 'chance' column, which is the test-set majority rate. answer_identity_family is the balanced four-class control and is the one of the three that carries information -- about task identity at the final token, not about answer identity.",
    "Whole-residual (all_positions) patching was NOT run. It needs the two runs to tokenize to the same length and, even then, position i holds a different token in the two runs wherever the evidence moved. --include-all-positions runs it as an explicit upper bound."
  ]
